content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-107 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22950",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration is 5.5 mm/s RMS on the bearing housing, so the applicable limit is HF-300 Figure 3. This is within Zone C, 4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS: 'Restricted - plan maintenance'. It is not in Zone D, 'Damage likely - stop the pump'.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Last month's 3.0 mm/s RMS reading was in Zone B, 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation'. The reported reading has therefore increased by 2.5 mm/s RMS and crossed the 4.5 mm/s RMS Zone B/Zone C boundary.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the 76 °C drive-end housing reading, the applicable limits are the HF-300 bearing-housing surface-temperature limits: normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C. The reading is 6 °C above normal, 4 °C below alarm and 14 °C below trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current evidence supports planned P2 maintenance rather than an immediate stop or temperature-driven P1: 5.5 mm/s RMS is Zone C rather than the manufacturer's highest severity zone, and 76 °C is not above the 80 °C alarm limit. SSP-07's immediate-stop rule and its rule requiring a priority-1 work order within the shift are therefore not triggered by these readings.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported. The manual's seal-leakage symptom and its mechanical-seal replacement action are therefore not established by this report; do not plan seal replacement on this evidence alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Investigate bearing wear first, together with misalignment: bearing wear is documented as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, matching the two abnormal findings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is the other common documented cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature and should be checked with a laser alignment tool.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is a documented cause of high bearing temperature; check the grease quantity before attributing the temperature rise solely to bearing damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation remain documented causes of high vibration; inspect the impeller and check NPSH if the bearing, grease and alignment checks do not explain the readings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Repeat the vibration-velocity measurement on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Confirm the drive-end housing-surface temperature. If vibration is classified in Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart; if bearing temperature rises above 80 °C, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check bearing grease quantity and investigate the operating conditions for cavitation by checking NPSH. Laser-check shaft alignment against parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm; record the actual values.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearings or the impeller require internal inspection, first apply the listed isolation and line-break controls. Use the back pull-out arrangement for rotating-assembly access; it can be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg, so use the required signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings and impeller and record any wear, noise or damage. If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair—HF3-512 at the drive end and HF3-510 at the non-drive end—rather than replacing only one bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket. On reassembly, tighten disturbed fasteners with lightly oiled threads to the applicable values: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm; M10 seal gland nuts 25 Nm; M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser alignment again and verify parallel offset of 0.05 mm and angular alignment of 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to routine service, record vibration on both housings, classify the highest result, and check bearing-housing temperature against the 70/80/90 °C limits. Maintain the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Have available for conditional bearing replacement; if replacement is triggered, install as part of a bearing pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Have available for conditional replacement together with the drive-end bearing when either bearing meets the manual's replacement condition.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, required only if the casing is opened; replace whenever casing opening occurs. Back pull-out access itself need not disturb the casing or pipework.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds SSP-07's 25 kg lifting threshold. Before lifting it, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If any subsequent vibration reading falls in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing temperature rises above the manufacturer's 80 °C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory if P-107 is confirmed to be on a chemically dosed line. The supplied dosing note identifies only P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, so it does not establish that this control applies to P-107; confirm the service before line break.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician per alignment task; repeat the alignment if work moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement as a pair: standard allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians if inspection confirms the manual's replacement condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "No conflicting numerical limits were identified. Use AQ-OM-300 Revision D for this AquaDyne HF-300 because it matches the reported model; the supplied evidence provides no serial-specific alternative for HF3-22950. SSP-07 Revision 3 also applies because it covers all pumps on site. The manual supplies the machine limits, while SSP-07 supplies the corresponding site controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The general chemical-PPE rule and the chemical-dosing asset note do not conflict: the PPE rule applies only when a line is chemically dosed, while the asset note expressly identifies P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line. It cannot by itself be extended to P-107.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the current non-drive-end vibration reading? The manual requires measurements on both housings and classification of the highest reading, so the supplied 5.5 mm/s RMS drive-end value establishes Zone C for that reading but does not prove it is the machine's highest reading. [C06, C07]",
    "Is P-107's actual service chemically dosed? This must be confirmed before line break to determine whether chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required; the provided dosing list covers P-101 to P-106 only. [C15, C16]",
    "What are the measured alignment values, grease condition and quantity, bearing wear/noise findings, impeller condition, and NPSH/cavitation findings? These are needed to select the root cause and decide whether bearing-pair replacement is required. [C09, C10]",
    "The manual calls for a grease-quantity check and an NPSH check, but the evidence provides neither a target grease quantity or grease specification nor NPSH acceptance data. Obtain the applicable values before adjusting grease or accepting the NPSH check. [C09]",
    "The standard labour table does not provide durations for the diagnostic inspections, so the total work-order duration cannot be fixed until the bearing, impeller, grease, alignment and NPSH findings establish the repair scope. [C09, C12]",
    "Figure 3 does not state which zone owns values exactly on a boundary. If a reading is exactly 2.8, 4.5 or 7.1 mm/s RMS, obtain the site/reliability engineer's classification rather than inferring it; the reported 3.0 and 5.5 readings are not boundary values. [C07]"
  ]
}
